id: thrust
name: Thrust
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCost: 0
attacking: false
requiresTarget: true
thrust: true
usageLimit: 1/round
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Shove an Opponent in your Melee Range. A Clash of Strike against their Strike or
  Dodge; win and you either blow them back half your Might in Squares, with any
  Collision Damage doubled, or wrestle them to the ground.
text: >
  Thrust Maneuver [1/Round]: You strike an Opponent to knock them off-balance or
  blow them away.
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –KP Cost: N/A
  –Exploitable: N/A
  –Effect: Target an Opponent within your Melee Range and make a Clash (Strike vs
  Strike/Dodge) against them. If you win, choose one of the effects below to apply:

  * Push Back. The target is moved a number of Squares equal to 1/2 of your Might.
    The movement is in a straight line and away from you. Double any Collision
    Damage they suffer due to this movement.
  * Knock Prone. Make a second Clash (Impulsive/Corporeal). If you win, they are
    knocked Prone. If you lose, they suffer from the Guard Down Combat Condition
    until the end of your turn.

---

# No script. The whole of this Maneuver is two Clashes and a choice between them,
# and a script can neither open a Clash nor wait for one to land - so `thrust: true`
# hands it to the code that can, the same way `grapple` and `launch` are handled.
#
# What it comes to:
#   - the first Clash is a Grapple Check in every respect but its name: Strike
#     against their Strike or Dodge, their choice, and a tie goes to them
#   - winning offers the two effects as buttons on the card, because "choose one of
#     the effects below" is a choice made after the roll rather than before it
#   - Push Back says how many Squares and in which direction, and arms the collision
#     button at double - "double any Collision Damage they suffer due to this
#     movement"
#   - Knock Prone opens the second Clash, and that one lands either way: Prone if
#     you win it, Guard Down on them if you do not
#
# Losing the first Clash does nothing at all. The entry says what winning buys and
# says nothing about losing, so nothing is what happens - this Maneuver is not
# Exploitable and there is no second sentence to build.
#
# --- What is not built, and why -----------------------------------------------
#
# The movement. "The movement is in a straight line and away from you" is a fact
# about the map, and this system moves nobody: the card says how far and which way,
# and the token is the player's to drag. What they hit on the way is the collision,
# which is a question the card does ask.
#
# "1/2 of your Might" is read as half, rounded down, because every other half in
# these rules is - the Minimum Ki Point Cost is "half the Profile's listed cost,
# rounded down" and the Ki Wager limit is half your Capacity the same way. The entry
# does not say, and this is the reading that matches the book's habit.
#
# --- One thing the entry leaves open ------------------------------------------
#
# "Make a second Clash (Impulsive/Corporeal)." The first Clash in this entry is
# written "(Strike vs Strike/Dodge)", where `vs` separates the two sides and the
# slash offers a choice. This one has no `vs` - so the slash is read here as the
# same slash: a choice, offered to each side, of which of the two Saving Throws
# they answer with.
#
# The other reading is that the Initiator rolls Impulsive and the Defender rolls
# Corporeal. If that is the one meant, the change is one line - the `choose` on the
# save Clash stops asking and the two sides are fixed.
